@startuml render-preview
|Editor|
start
:Open a project without waiting for the renderer;
:Become interactive for editing;
|Renderer|
:Start in the background, whether or not
the preview pane is open;
|Editor|
:Show "Not yet checked" for every block
until it has been rendered;
repeat
  :Take the next block, the open block first;
  if (Can the block be rendered?) then (yes)
    |Renderer|
    :Render the block, off the editing path;
    if (Finished within 10 seconds?) then (yes)
      if (Render succeeded?) then (yes)
        |Editor|
        :Show the new preview and the block's render status;
      else (no)
        |Editor|
        :Keep the last preview, marked out of date;
        :Show the renderer's message and the block in the
        preview pane, labelled as a rendering problem;
      endif
    else (no)
      |Editor|
      :Abandon the render and report the block
      as "Not yet checked";
    endif
  else (no: invalid, or depends on !include)
    |Editor|
    :Keep the last preview, marked out of date;
  endif
  note right
    Editing on the canvas, outline and
    source continues throughout.
  end note
repeat while (A block is waiting or has changed?) is (yes)
->no;
stop
@enduml
